Original commit body from 7c94a2db0ea42d4272aee96fe50108c39f4c09a4:

Owner ruling 2026-10-25: delete it ("no dead code; no instrument without a
reader"). DataModel.kind was written by all four detectors and read by
nothing; its only serializer, DataModel.to_dict(), had no caller outside
its own test, so the value reached no output. The 2026-05-27 concept audit
kept it under three re-evaluation triggers, two of which could never fire
on a field nothing reads.

Removed: the enum (with its three-axis docstring), the field, to_dict()
(a second no-reader method), and the kind column of MODEL_BASE_CLASSES,
MODEL_DECORATORS and NAMING_PATTERNS. NAMING_PATTERNS now pairs each
pattern with the label it gives, which replaces the suffix if-chain and its
`pragma: no cover` else branch; the label is unchanged, because the first
matching pattern's suffix is the one the name ends with. label, framework,
confidence and rank_score are kept.

Tests: the 18 test_datamodels assertions on kind now assert the label the
same detector row produces (each test also asserts detection itself, so
none was kind-only); the to_dict test is deleted with the method; nine
DataModel(kind=...) constructors in test_sketch drop the argument.

Behaviour: none. `hypergumbo sketch` on a Django / Pydantic / dataclass /
naming-convention fixture is byte-identical before and after apart from
the cache-path footer. The .agent playbook's 2026-05-27 Examples entry is
governance-owned history and is left as it is.

